WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:05.555
Read an old institutional email or academic abstract. You may

00:00:05.555 --> 00:00:10.560
find the immaculate, depersonalized language we now accuse machines of inventing.

00:00:16.842 --> 00:00:21.562
Universities demand standard structure, impeccable polish and phrases approved

00:00:21.562 --> 00:00:26.282
by gatekeepers. Writers learn to hide any particular voice.

00:00:32.258 --> 00:00:36.455
When software produces the very language institutions rewarded,

00:00:36.455 --> 00:00:40.652
people suddenly decide that the sound itself is incriminating.

00:00:46.092 --> 00:00:49.744
A sentence pattern is not evidence of who conceived

00:00:49.744 --> 00:00:53.397
an idea, performed an experiment or understood a conclusion.

00:00:58.217 --> 00:01:02.412
What does this author know? Are the sources real?

00:01:02.412 --> 00:01:06.607
Can the argument survive direct examination? Those questions require judgment.

00:01:12.008 --> 00:01:15.804
The essay is about intellectual responsibility, not an

00:01:15.804 --> 00:01:19.600
entitlement to publish inaccuracies in a distinctive style.
